  "objectives": [
    "Describe the apparent path of Mars across the night sky during a retrograde episode, including normal eastward drift, a temporary westward loop, and return to eastward motion.",
    "Explain apparent retrograde motion in the heliocentric model as a consequence of Earth overtaking a slower-moving outer planet.",
    "Contrast geocentric epicycle-based explanations with the simpler heliocentric explanation for retrograde motion.",
    "Predict when retrograde motion will occur for an outer planet from the relative orbital positions of Earth and that planet.",
    "Compare the retrograde loops of Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn and explain why more distant planets show smaller apparent loops."
